{
  "An application menu bar (File, Edit, View) and a context menu that opens on right-click. Both use the same menu items, which support submenus, check and radio items, shortcuts and access keys.": "",
  "MenuBar": "MenuBar",
  "A `MenuBar` takes its top-level items as `items`, and the `items` of each one define its menu. `&File` assigns Alt+F to open File. Left and Right move along the bar and, while a menu is open, to the next menu. Escape returns to the bar.": "",
  "Submenus, check items, radio items and shortcuts": "",
  "An item with `items` opens a submenu at its side. Right (Left on right-to-left pages), Enter or Space opens it, Left and Escape close it, and hovering opens it after a short delay. `checked` creates a check item, and `checked` with a `group` creates one choice in a set, shown with a dot. `shortcut` is displayed at the end of the item, so register the key separately with `addShortcut`. The same items work in a `Button` menu.": "",
  "The label. `&Copy` makes C select the item while the menu is open (Alt+C on a top-level menu bar item).": "",
  "An icon at the start, and a tooltip.": "",
  "A key combination displayed at the end (`Ctrl+S`). It is for display only, so register the key with `addShortcut`.": "",
  "A second, dimmer text after the label that distinguishes the item, such as a folder name. It is part of the item's name and never a key.": "",
  "A submenu that opens at the side.": "",
  "A check item (`menuitemcheckbox`).": "Onay öğesi (`menuitemcheckbox`).",
  "With `checked`, one choice in a group (`menuitemradio`), shown with a dot.": "",
  "Dims the item so it cannot be selected, or removes it.": "",
  "Colors the item with a kit tone (`danger` for destructive actions). A toolbar button moved into the overflow menu keeps its tone.": "",
  "Occurs when the item is selected, after the menu closes. `e`: `{ item, source, event }`.": "",
  "ContextMenu": "ContextMenu",
  "A `ContextMenu` opens at the pointer when its target is right-clicked, and at the focused element with the Menu key or Shift+F10. `onOpening` receives the element (`e.target`) and builds the items for it, in this case for a row in a list. Setting `e.cancel = true` leaves the browser's own menu. The menu closes on Escape or a click outside. When the page scrolls, it follows the element it opened on and closes once that element is out of view.": "",
  "attachContextMenu": "attachContextMenu",
  "Moves focus into the menu bar (one Tab stop) and out of it.": "",
  "On the bar, moves to the previous or next top-level item. In a menu, moves to the adjacent menu or closes a submenu (Right opens one). These keys are mirrored on right-to-left pages.": "",
  "On the bar, opens the menu on its first item. Up opens it on the last item.": "",
  "In a menu, moves between items and wraps at the ends.": "",
  "Moves to the next item that starts with that letter. An item's `&` key selects it.": "",
  "Opens the top-level item with that `&` key (Control + Option on Apple platforms).": "",
  "Closes a submenu, then the menu, and returns to where it opened.": "",
  "Moves focus to the menu bar when `focusOnF10` is set.": "",
  "Opens a context menu at the focused element.": "Odaktaki öğede bağlam menüsü açar.",
  "`role=\"menubar\"` named by `label`. Top-level items are `menuitem` elements with `aria-haspopup` and `aria-expanded`, and the bar is one Tab stop (roving tabindex).": "",
  "`role=\"menu\"`. Items are `menuitem`, `menuitemcheckbox` or `menuitemradio` with `aria-checked`. Disabled items have `aria-disabled` and remain reachable.": "",
  "The item has `aria-haspopup=\"menu\"` and `aria-expanded`. The submenu opens next to it, focus moves in and returns when it closes.": "",
  "A menu opened from the keyboard focuses its first item, and a menu opened with the pointer focuses the menu itself. Closing returns focus.": "",
  "The shortcut text is part of the item's name. Access keys are exposed through `aria-keyshortcuts` on top-level items.": "",
  "Menus have no strings of their own. Every label, shortcut and name comes from your items, so they follow your own translations. A function in `text` updates immediately when the language changes.": "",
  "The menu bar, its row and a top-level item (`aria-expanded=\"true\"` while open).": "",
  "The context menu, which has no box of its own, and the point it opens at.": "",
  "A menu (shared with Button), an item and a separator.": "",
  "The parts of an item.": "Öğenin parçaları.",
  "The height of the bar and of a top-level item.": "",
  "Units: the bar, a top-level item with its box per state (`hover`, `pressed`, `open`, `disabled`, `focus`), its icon, and its access key indicator (`shown`).": "",
  "Menu items, shared with the Button menu: the item unit in each state (`highlight`, `pressed`, `focus`, `checked`, `disabled`, `first`, `last`, each tone and `<tone>-highlight`), the row height, and text wrapping.": "",
  "Units: the item column, the leading indicator and icon, the check and radio marks, and the separator between groups.": "",
  "Units: the item text, its description, the shortcut and the submenu arrow.": "",
  "MenuBar props": "MenuBar prop'ları",
  "The top-level items, whose `items` define the menus they open. A top-level item without `items` runs its `click`.": "",
  "The accessible name of the bar. This is the same property as `text`.": "",
  "F10 moves focus to the bar from anywhere on the page. This is off by default because browsers use F10.": "",
  "While a menu is open, hovering another top-level item opens its menu, and hovering an item opens its submenu.": "",
  "ContextMenu props": "ContextMenu prop'ları",
  "The commands. `onOpening` can provide different ones for each element.": "",
  "Its parent": "",
  "The element the menu belongs to. If not set, this is the element the `ContextMenu` is placed in.": "",
  "The accessible name of the menu.": "",
  "The Menu key and Shift+F10 open the menu at the focused element.": "",
  "Scrolling the element out of view closes the menu. Until then, the menu follows the element.": "",
  "Hovering an item opens its submenu.": "",
  "`false` shows the browser's own menu.": "",
  "The top-level item whose menu is open.": "",
  "The element the menu was last opened on.": "",
  "The element the menu listens on.": "",
  "Opens a top-level item's menu with focus on its first item.": "",
  "Closes the open menu.": "Açık menüyü kapatır.",
  "Opens the menu programmatically, at `{ x, y }` or at an element.": "",
  "Your items can be plain or reactive, and the menu reads them as they are. After changing them in place, call `refresh()`. The bar, the open menu and its submenus update.": "",
  "Attaches a menu to an element or component. `items` can be a function of the opening event (`e.target`). Returns a function that removes the menu.": "",
  "On both components, occurs when an item is selected, after its own `click`.": "",
  "Occurs before the menu opens. `e`: `{ target, items, cancel, byKeyboard, event, source }`. Set `e.items` for the element, or set `e.cancel = true`.": "",
  "`escape`, `outside`, `focus` or `code`.": "`escape`, `outside`, `focus` ya da `code`."
}
